t":"# Plan: CSV import for tinycsv\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development-parallel (recommended) to implement this plan task-by-task.\n\n## Dependency overview\n\n- Task 1: none\n- Task 2: none\n- Task 3: none\n\n## Task 1: read_header\n\n**Depends on:** none\n\n- Consumes: nothing\n- Produces: `read_header(path: str) -> list[str]` in `header.py`\n\n**Step 1: Write the failing test** — `tests/test_header.py`, asserting the header\nof a two-column CSV comes back as `[\"a\", \"b\"]`.\n\n**Step 2: Implement** `header.py` so the test passes. Commit.\n\n## Task 2: create_table\n\n**Depends on:** none\n\n- Consumes: nothing\n- Produces: `create_table(conn, name: str, columns: list[str]) -> None` in `schema.py`\n\n**Step 1: Write the failing test** — `tests/test_schema.py`, asserting the table\nexists with TEXT columns after the call.\n\n**Step 2: Implement** `schema.py` so the test passes. Commit.\n\n## Task 3: load_rows\n\n**Depends on:** none\n\n- Consumes: nothing\n- Produces: `load_rows(conn, name: str, rows: list[list[str]]) -> int` in `rows.py`\n\n**Step 1: Write the failing test** — `tests/test_rows.py`, asserting the returned\ncount matches the number of inserted rows.\n\n**Step 2: Implement** `rows.py` so the test passes. Commit.\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
