{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdYcuK7zXht8JDb5Uobq3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015PisWAHThKd9bN6CXRzxby","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jacek-prjs-skills/269c2167-adeb-455e-8871-4018c0077d3f/scratchpad/probes/probeB-run/.claude/worktrees/csv-import-integration-task-1/.superpowers/sdd/task-1-report.md","content":"# Task 1 report: read_header\n\n## Implemented\n- `header.py`: `read_header(path: str) -> list[str]` reads the first row of a CSV file\n  and returns it as a list of column names, using `csv.reader` (stdlib) for correct\n  field splitting.\n- `tests/test_header.py`: writes a two-column CSV (`a,b\\n1,2\\n`) to a tmp_path file\n  and asserts `read_header(path) == [\"a\", \"b\"]`.\n\n## TDD evidence\n\nRED (before header.py existed):\n```\n$ uv run --no-project python -m pytest -q tests/test_header.py\nImportError while importing test module '.../tests/test_header.py'.\nE   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'header'\n1 error in 0.05s\n```\n\nGREEN (after implementing header.py):\n```\n$ uv run --no-project python -m pytest -q\n..                                                                       [100%]\n2 passed in 0.01s\n```\n(2 = new test_header.py test + pre-existing test_tinycsv.py test, both green, no warnings)\n\n## Files changed\n- `header.py` (new)\n- `tests/test_header.py` (new)\n- Did not touch `tinycsv.py` or `tests/test_tinycsv.py`.\n\n## Self-review\n- Scope: only `read_header` implemented, no CSV dialect/encoding options, no quoting\n  config beyond what stdlib `csv.reader` gives by default — matches brief (YAGNI).\n- Test hygiene: single focused test, tmp_path fixture (no leftover files), pristine\n  pytest output (no warnings).\n- `newline=\"\"` on `open()` is the standard/required idiom for Python's `csv` module\n  (avoids universal-newline translation interfering with the CSV parser) — not\n  speculative, it's the documented correct usage.\n- Auto-formatter (ruff, per project Stop hook) inserted a blank line between the\n  module docstring and `import csv` — reviewed, harmless, kept.\n\n## Concerns\nNone. Task is small and self-contained; no ambiguity encountered.\n\n## Commit\n- `3249e77` \"Add read_header for CSV column names\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_read_input_tokens":30686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":404,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RvYBeU8hprpmoYxorU9jDG","session_id":"7183153f-7116-4943-8f43-18f1f1380ed3","uuid":"a80e1bd1-90d1-4050-a9cd-207cc909af53","timestamp":"2026-07-30T17:15:52.931Z","request_id":"req_011CdYcuHgfe2NUjxuvTkfPp","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement Task 1: read_header"}
