{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdYcwgoHGrQqYyLTcPvjM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3522,"cache_read_input_tokens":89731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3522},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7183153f-7116-4943-8f43-18f1f1380ed3","uuid":"1b69d3e9-41ed-4158-9ef1-6016b7ac8158","timestamp":"2026-07-30T17:16:18.341Z","request_id":"req_011CdYcweX7MaQZhogCHxmNG"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdYcw6rrbCDWYqgFkuTXL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013XfXBrmKe4dyvGrQTRh95D","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jacek-prjs-skills/269c2167-adeb-455e-8871-4018c0077d3f/scratchpad/probes/probeB-run/.claude/worktrees/csv-import-integration-task-3/.superpowers/sdd/task-3-report.md","content":"# Task 3 report: load_rows\n\n## Implemented\n`rows.py`: `load_rows(conn, name: str, rows: list[list[str]]) -> int`.\nBuilds an `INSERT INTO {name} VALUES (?,...)` statement sized to the width of the\nfirst row, runs it via `conn.executemany`, commits, and returns `len(rows)`.\nEmpty `rows` list returns `0` without touching the DB.\n\nNo validation, type coercion, or batching beyond a single `executemany` call —\nkept to what the brief and YAGNI require.\n\n## TDD evidence\n\nRED:\n```\n$ uv run --no-project python -m pytest -q tests/test_rows.py\nERROR collecting tests/test_rows.py\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rows'\n1 error in 0.06s\n```\n\nGREEN:\n```\n$ uv run --no-project python -m pytest -q\n..                                                                       [100%]\n2 passed in 0.04s\n```\n(2 = the new test_rows.py test + the pre-existing test_tinycsv.py test, both pass, no warnings.)\n\n## Files changed\n- `rows.py` (new)\n- `tests/test_rows.py` (new)\n- Did not touch `tinycsv.py` or `tests/test_tinycsv.py`.\n\n## Test design note\nThe test creates its own target table directly with raw SQL\n(`CREATE TABLE t (a, b)`) via the real sqlite3 connection returned by\n`tinycsv.connect`, per the brief's guidance to avoid depending on the sibling\n`create_table` task in `schema.py`. It asserts both the returned count and the\nactual row count in the table (`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM t`), which stays within\nscope — it verifies the one behavior the function has, not extra scenarios.\n\n## Self-review\n- Completeness: brief's two steps (failing test, then implementation) both done, matching the exact signature and file names specified.\n- Quality: single small function, no unused imports, docstring present per repo convention.\n- YAGNI: no schema introspection, no column-name handling, no error handling for row-width mismatches or SQL injection on table name — none of these were requested and the brief describes \"a simple insert-and-count.\"\n- Test hygiene: pristine `pytest -q` output, no warnings, no skipped tests, no dependency on sibling tasks' files.\n\n## Concerns\n- `name` (table name) is interpolated directly into the SQL string with an f-string. This is standard for identifiers in sqlite3 (parameter binding only covers values, not identifiers) and is consistent with how a minimal loader would call this internally with a trusted, already-validated table name — not an issue for this task's scope, but worth knowing if `name` ever becomes user-supplied without validation upstream.\n- Row width is taken from `rows[0]`; if callers ever pass rows of inconsistent length, `executemany` will raise a sqlite3 error naturally — no explicit handling added, per YAGNI.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":31227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":358,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LyXhnTgPmxcvEnx6GvvoKg","session_id":"7183153f-7116-4943-8f43-18f1f1380ed3","uuid":"dd2fd896-f6d7-475b-a98d-f1a235f68d14","timestamp":"2026-07-30T17:16:20.054Z","request_id":"req_011CdYcw5M4zk3jgN9wFqebD","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement Task 3: load_rows"}
