{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KfLeZWijtDGDVJFaScD9at","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Task 1 report: read_header\n2\t\n3\t## Implemented\n4\t- `header.py`: `read_header(path: str) -> list[str]` reads the first row of a CSV file\n5\t  and returns it as a list of column names, using `csv.reader` (stdlib) for correct\n6\t  field splitting.\n7\t- `tests/test_header.py`: writes a two-column CSV (`a,b\\n1,2\\n`) to a tmp_path file\n8\t  and asserts `read_header(path) == [\"a\", \"b\"]`.\n9\t\n10\t## TDD evidence\n11\t\n12\tRED (before header.py existed):\n13\t```\n14\t$ uv run --no-project python -m pytest -q tests/test_header.py\n15\tImportError while importing test module '.../tests/test_header.py'.\n16\tE   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'header'\n17\t1 error in 0.05s\n18\t```\n19\t\n20\tGREEN (after implementing header.py):\n21\t```\n22\t$ uv run --no-project python -m pytest -q\n23\t..                                                                       [100%]\n24\t2 passed in 0.01s\n25\t```\n26\t(2 = new test_header.py test + pre-existing test_tinycsv.py test, both green, no warnings)\n27\t\n28\t## Files changed\n29\t- `header.py` (new)\n30\t- `tests/test_header.py` (new)\n31\t- Did not touch `tinycsv.py` or `tests/test_tinycsv.py`.\n32\t\n33\t## Self-review\n34\t- Scope: only `read_header` implemented, no CSV dialect/encoding options, no quoting\n35\t  config beyond what stdlib `csv.reader` gives by default — matches brief (YAGNI).\n36\t- Test hygiene: single focused test, tmp_path fixture (no leftover files), pristine\n37\t  pytest output (no warnings).\n38\t- `newline=\"\"` on `open()` is the standard/required idiom for Python's `csv` module\n39\t  (avoids universal-newline translation interfering with the CSV parser) — not\n40\t  speculative, it's the documented correct usage.\n41\t- Auto-formatter (ruff, per project Stop hook) inserted a blank line between the\n42\t  module docstring and `import csv` — re